 ### Cross-campaign agent identity
 
 A campaign always contains 10 production agents. The workflow's local campaign slots remain 01–10 only as execution positions. Each production session also receives a durable global agent number from `state/campaign/global_agent_counter.json`: campaign 1 uses 01–10, campaign 2 uses 11–20, campaign 3 uses 21–30, and so on. This prevents cross-session identity reset and makes long-run learning history easier to reconstruct. Structural miniature runs use `MINI-01`, `MINI-02`, etc. and do not consume production identities.
+
+
+## Selection-basis record (attributing selection vs execution)
+
+**Problem (agent 01, run 43657769763):** per-activation records capture *execution* quality (verdict, independent-verification MATCH, determinism) but not *selection* quality (which alternatives were open and what the chosen cell actually delivered). A `RETAIN (verified)` label therefore conflates "the chosen cell was executed well" with "the selector chose well", and a future audit cannot attribute the selector's effect.
+
+**Convention:** every frontier-cell activation records exactly one `selection_basis_record` object in its durable agent record. It is descriptive and qualitative — it assigns no numerical score.
+
+| Field | Type | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `alternatives_compared` | list of task_id | Candidate task_ids that were OPEN for the role at selection time (authoritative source: contract `selection_basis.compared_against`, which lists the top candidates including the chosen one). |
+| `chosen_task` | task_id | The task actually selected. |
+| `was_flagged_priority` | boolean | True iff the chosen task was the single pre-declared highest-value unresolved item in `LEARNING_STATE` ("Next" / frontier qualification) — i.e. selection was driven by an explicit ranking, not mere availability. |
+| `realized_information_gain` | HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW / NONE | Qualitative information gain actually delivered by the chosen cell (falsification, uncertainty reduction, new independent evidence, repaired defect, new capability). |
+| `information_gain_evidence` | text | One-line citation of the durable evidence for the gain (verdict + the specific uncertainty closed). |
+| `selection_attribution` | RANKING / ENUMERATION / MIXED / UNRESOLVED | Derived label (rule below). |
+
+**Attribution rule (how an audit distinguishes the two effects):**
+
+- `RANKING` — `was_flagged_priority` is true AND `realized_information_gain` is HIGH/MEDIUM AND the chosen cell closed the *specific* uncertainty it was flagged for while the recorded alternatives addressed *different* uncertainties. The selector's choice mattered.
+- `ENUMERATION` — the realized gain is attributable to a distinct cell/class becoming available (breadth), and the recorded alternatives were substitutes for the same uncertainty. The menu mattered, not the pick.
+- `MIXED` — both a flagged-priority pick and a breadth effect are evidenced.
+- `UNRESOLVED` — the recorded fields are insufficient to separate the two.
+
+This separation is what the success criterion requires: using only the recorded data, an audit can tell whether a positive outcome came from enumeration (a useful menu) or ranking (choosing the right item).
+
+**Worked example (existing resolved cell R-001, agent 02, run 43657769763):**
+
+```json
+{
+  "alternatives_compared": ["R-001", "R-002", "R-003", "R-005"],
+  "chosen_task": "R-001",
+  "was_flagged_priority": true,
+  "realized_information_gain": "HIGH",
+  "information_gain_evidence": "Closed the explicitly flagged cost-robustness qualification: 16/17 zero-cost EDGE cells COST_ROBUST, a-priori 'majority fragile' prediction refuted, independently verified (fresh walk_forward+noise_benchmark MATCH).",
+  "selection_attribution": "RANKING"
+}
+```
+
+Why `RANKING`: LEARNING_STATE's active-delta "Next" explicitly named cost-robustness as the decision-relevant qualification; the recorded alternatives (R-002 holding period, R-003 volatility gate, R-005 sizing) address *different* uncertainties, so choosing R-001 was a ranking decision that closed the specific flagged gap. Contrast: a new-signal-class cell whose gain is simply "one more class eliminated" would be recorded `ENUMERATION` (or `MIXED`) because any deferred cell would have added breadth.

